# ComposeServer MCP Surface — agent-facing sibling of the WS endpoint; PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-MCP]

> The MCP surface is the AGENT-FACING sibling of [SPEC:CXC-WS]: where a browser tab becomes a live bus
> peer over WS carrying raw namespace traffic, an Intelligence becomes a live bus peer over MCP carrying
> TOOL CALLS. Transport is an implementation detail ([plt.cio:SPEC:DP-CIO-6]) — the wire underneath MCP's
> JSON-RPC (stdio, SSE, streamable-HTTP) is swappable connector config, never a fork in the contract. ONE
> aggregating router per ComposeServer enumerates every loaded plugin's DECLARED tools — one typed
> pydantic manifest, the same one that already derives a plugin's config form and announce
> ([CXC-CS-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]), now ALSO derives its MCP tool schema — and exposes them
> per-plugin-namespaced (`fingerprint.enroll`, `time.set_zone`). A tool call ENCODES to a bus publish,
> table-driven from the tool's own declared schema; a read/subscription tool DECODES bus state back to
> the agent, either directly (a retained value) or via [SPEC:CXC-BUS-QUERY]'s round-trip idiom. The
> umbrella NEVER derives a new semantic fact from what it forwards — [DX-CONNECTOR-FORWARDS-NEVER-TRANSFORMS]
> applies here exactly as it does to every other connector — so ComposeServer stays supervisor, never
> mediator. A plugin whose surface is inherently separate MAY declare its own endpoint; that is the
> knowing exception, never the default.

---

