## 2. The umbrella, ratified — one aggregating surface, not per-plugin endpoints by default

### [CXC-MCP-UMBRELLA-RATIFIED] MUST aggregate every loaded plugin's declared tools behind ONE MCP surface per ComposeServer; a per-plugin endpoint is the exception, never the default

- requirement: (MUST, testable) ComposeServer MUST expose plugin capabilities to an MCP client through ONE
  aggregating router, not one MCP endpoint per plugin. A tool declared by plugin `fingerprint` and a tool
  declared by plugin `time` MUST both be reachable over the SAME MCP session, namespaced by their
  declaring plugin (`fingerprint.enroll`, `time.set_zone`), never requiring the client to know or dial a
  different endpoint per capability.
- why: mirrors [CXC-CS-MICROKERNEL]'s own test applied one layer up — any capability that CAN share the
  umbrella MUST, and the residue after the true exceptions ([CXC-MCP-FORK-EXCEPTION]) defines the
  legitimate default. An MCP client that had to dial N endpoints for N plugins would be re-deriving the
  per-service self-connect sprawl [CXC-CBK-MQTT-INDEPENDENT] already collapsed at the transport layer,
  one abstraction level higher.
- verify-machine: a test ComposeServer with >=2 loaded plugins, each declaring >=1 tool, exposes ALL
  declared tools over ONE MCP session's tool-list response; no plugin's tools require a second connection.
- verify-human: none required — this node's failure surface is fully machine-observable.
- status: proposed
- provenance: david-ratified-by-concurrence — David's actual word (2026-08-25): "I endorse your MCP
  approach." This is the whole of David's ratification; it was given in response to the umbrella-over-
  per-plugin-endpoints design as proposed in the dispatch that produced this spec. The elaboration in
  this node's `requirement` and `why` properties is the author's framing of the agreed ruling, not a
  tenant-scoping, the tool-declaration schema shape, the thin-router mechanics, the fork-exception — is
  `architect-recommendation` (David explicitly delegated: "you don't need me to fully spec it out"), and
  each such node below carries that tag distinctly rather than borrowing this one's ratified weight.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MCP]
- see-also: [CXC-MCP-ROUTER-MECHANICS], [CXC-MCP-FORK-EXCEPTION], [CXC-CS-MICROKERNEL]

