## 4. Endpoint topology — one umbrella endpoint per ComposeServer, tenant-scoped per session

### [CXC-MCP-ENDPOINT-TOPOLOGY] MUST run ONE MCP connector instance per ComposeServer; a session selects its tenant post-connect, mirroring [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE]'s PRE-BINDING -> select -> BOUND shape — DECIDED for v1

- requirement: (MUST, testable) a ComposeServer instance MUST stand up exactly ONE MCP connector,
  spanning every tenant it hosts, rather than one MCP connector per tenant. A newly connected MCP session
  starts unbound (no tenant selected) and MUST select a tenant before any tool that touches a tenant bus
  is reachable — the same PRE-BINDING/BOUND shape [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE] already specifies for the WS
  connector, reused here rather than re-derived, because inventing a second binding state machine for the
  same underlying [CXC-CS-MULTI-TENANCY] boundary would be exactly the "designed too specifically"
  failure [CXC-VISION-ANNOUNCE-BIND]'s `design-check` warns against.
- resolved-2026-08-25: this was the architect's LEAN against a genuinely defensible alternative (one MCP
  endpoint per tenant, [DD-MCP-ENDPOINT-PER-TENANT]) recorded rather than silently foreclosed. Per
  [DEC-MCP-DD-RESOLVED-2026-08-25], the fork is now DECIDED: umbrella-per-ComposeServer, tenant-scoped
  per session — maximal reuse of [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE]'s already-settled binding lifecycle and
  [CXC-CS-LOADER-PUBLISHES-ANNOUNCE]'s derived-announce spine, over forking a divergent per-tenant model.
  The per-tenant-endpoint alternative is REJECTED for v1 (RE-LITIGABLE per [DD-MCP-ENDPOINT-PER-TENANT]'s
  own invalidating_assumption). The requirement accordingly moves SHOULD -> MUST.
- tenant-selection-surface: the CONCRETE SHAPE of the tenant-selection tool (a dedicated control-plane
  tool such as `_server.select_tenant`, an MCP-native "resource" listing, or a connection-time parameter
  analogous to WS's deep-link) remains an implementation detail this spec does not fix — but the
  endpoint-topology fork it used to be bundled with is no longer open: see [DD-MCP-ENDPOINT-PER-TENANT]
  (rejected for v1) and [DD-MCP-TRANSPORT-CHOICE] (streamable-HTTP chosen for v1). This node specifies
  only that SOME selection step MUST exist and MUST precede any tenant-scoped tool call, not its concrete
  shape.
- verify-machine: a fresh MCP session's tool-list (or tool-invoke) surface exposes NO tenant-scoped tool
  until a tenant-selection step completes; after selection, exactly that tenant's aggregated tool set
  becomes reachable.
- verify-human: an operator connects a fresh MCP client against a ComposeServer hosting >=2 tenants and
  confirms no tenant's tools are invokable before an explicit selection, and that selecting tenant A never
  exposes or invokes tenant B's plugin instances.
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — the v1 topology per [DEC-MCP-DD-RESOLVED-2026-08-25]; re-litigable only per
  [DD-MCP-ENDPOINT-PER-TENANT]'s own invalidating_assumption (real multi-tenant use showing agents hold
  one long-lived tenant binding).
- provenance: architect-recommendation — per the dispatch's explicit delegation; ratified as the decided
  v1 topology by [DEC-MCP-DD-RESOLVED-2026-08-25] (David delegated the mechanism ratify: "you don't need
  me to fully spec it out").
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MCP]
- see-also: [CXC-WS-LIFECYCLE], [CXC-MCP-TENANT-BOUNDARY], [DD-MCP-ENDPOINT-PER-TENANT], [CXC-CS-MULTI-TENANCY], [DEC-MCP-DD-RESOLVED-2026-08-25]

