**Version**: 0.2 — 2026-08-25, corpus-hygiene revision reconciling this spec's text with
[DEC-MCP-DD-RESOLVED-2026-08-25] (which ratified all three forks after the umbrella build landed).
[CXC-MCP-ENDPOINT-TOPOLOGY] moves `proposed` -> `decided` (SHOULD -> MUST): umbrella-per-ComposeServer,
tenant-scoped per session, per-tenant-endpoint alternative rejected. [DD-MCP-ENDPOINT-PER-TENANT] moves
`open` -> `decided` (rejected for v1, re-litigable). [DD-MCP-TRANSPORT-CHOICE] moves `open` -> `decided`
(streamable-HTTP for v1, stdio degenerate-supported). [DD-MCP-AUTH-GATE] stays `deferred` but now names
the LAN-only-bind guard ([CXC-MCP-BOUNDARIES] row 11, MCP-V10) as load-bearing rather than aspirational,
since v1's decided wire is network-transported. Previously version 0.1, 2026-08-25, initial authoring from
the architect's dispatch. `[CXC-MCP-UMBRELLA-RATIFIED]` carries David's `david-ratified-by-concurrence`
ruling ("I endorse your MCP approach"); every other node is `architect-recommendation` per the dispatch's
explicit delegation. The load-bearing deliverable, [CXC-MCP-TOOL-DECLARATION], carries full build-spec
MUST/SHOULD + verify-machine/verify-human precision so a fan-out of future per-plugin adaptations can
implement against it without guessing; session-lifecycle mechanics are specified as a
MUST-mirror-[SPEC:CXC-WS] requirement rather than independently re-derived.

**Status**: Draft — the three forks named in v0.1 are now decided/confirmed per
[DEC-MCP-DD-RESOLVED-2026-08-25]; still awaiting architect/David ratify on every remaining
`architect-recommendation`-tagged node generally, per the dispatch's own instruction that only the
umbrella-over-per-plugin choice itself carries David's concurrence. ⚠ [CXC-MCP-EVIDENCE]'s
`evidence-connector-module` slot still reads EMPTY, claiming `composeio/transport_mcp.py` does not exist on
`origin/main` as of this spec's authoring — that file now exists on `origin/main` (landed the same day,
commit `d95aee1` and its ancestors); this corpus-hygiene pass did NOT update that evidence slot (out of
scope for the three requested edits) and it is flagged here so it is not read as still true.

*[SPEC:CXC-MCP] — the ComposeServer MCP umbrella surface. Agent-facing sibling of [SPEC:CXC-WS].*
